        "original_id": "4e9504f1-00a6-5b9f-80a4-86de587a3170",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jim Harrison, Dorree Cooper\n- Products: Legends of the Fall, Legends of the Fall novella\n- Places: Montana\n- Topics: American writing, family, nature, history, war, love, Academy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Jim Harrison was born on December 11, 1937, and he was an American writer known for poetry, fiction, reviews, essays about the outdoors, and writing about food.\n- The 1979 novella Legends of the Fall was written by Jim Harrison.\n- The film Legends of the Fall is based on Jim Harrison's 1979 novella of the same title.\n- Legends of the Fall is about three brothers and their father living in the wilderness and plains of Montana in the early 20th century.\n- Legends of the Fall portrays how the family's lives are affected by nature, history, war, and love.\n- Dorree Cooper was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Art Direction for the film Legends of the Fall.\n- Jim Harrison died on March 26, 2016.",
